Looking at the curve starting at B: it arcs over the top and down the right side. At the first crossing (with the straight line C–D), staying on the same smooth curve means following it as it spirals inward (down, around the bottom, and up the left side). At the second crossing with the line C–D, again staying on the same curve (not turning onto the line), the spiral continues inward and terminates at the inner endpoint A.

Thus, starting at B and never switching curves at crossings, the endpoint reached is A.

\boxed{A}
